    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0424" n="414" xml:id="pg414"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.935: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)<anchor n="86"
                        xml:id="d353-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-09-29T17:00:00-05:00">September 29, 1948—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1371. For Embassy, Casaday and Parker. State and Treas sympathetic Emb desire for
                    flexibility and Emb concern re possibility sudden and severe break in rate
                    (Embtel 1735<anchor n="87" xml:id="d353-f2"/> rptd Shanghai 829). Because
                    importance possible new rate on Army-Navy expenditures and implications for ECA
                    special account, which latter is NAC interest here, would appreciate more info
                    prior consideration your recommendation. Transmit alternative rate formulas
                    under consideration for possible approach Chinese Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d353-f1" n="86" type="source" xml:id="d353-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Consul General at Shanghai as No. 1676.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d353-f2" n="87" xml:id="d353-f2-content">
